          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#in_set_theory In set theory
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≡
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \equiv
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %strong quotient set
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≡
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \equiv
            is the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ≡
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S/{\equiv}
            whose elements are the elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            but where two elements are now considered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equal
            if in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            they were merely equivalent.
          %p
            If changing the definition of equality like this is not allowed in the given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} foundations
            of mathematics, then one can still define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ≡
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S/{\equiv}
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %ul
            %li
              In
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/material+set+theory"} material set theory
              the definition is as follows:
              #eq:setdef.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ≡
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⇔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∃
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi S
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      A \in S/{\equiv} \;\Leftrightarrow\; \exists (x: S),\; A = \{y: S \;\mid\; x \equiv y\}
            %li
              In
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structural+set+theory"} structural set theory
              the definition is slightly different, because sets are not elements of sets and one cannot in general compare sets for strict equality.
          %p If there are also no (extensional) power sets in the foundations of mathematics, then there are two alternatives:
          %ul
            %li
              One could use
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/setoids"} setoids
              (in which case, perhaps one would do better to change your terminology as described there).
            %li
              One could just include the existence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+objects"} quotient objects
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              as an axiom (the
              = succeed "." do
                %strong axiom of quotient sets
          %p
            The latter is the case if one assumes that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Set
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
            or a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            as given by
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giraud%27s+axioms"} Giraud's axioms
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The weaker version of the axiom of quotient sets is the one which states that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+category"} coherent category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                is a
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+equivalence+relation"} internal equivalence relation
                on a set
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≡
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \equiv
                of the Cartesian product
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times A
                satisfying reflexivity, transitivity, and symmetry, has a quotient set
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ≡
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A/\equiv
            %li
              %p
                The stronger version of the axiom of quotient sets states that every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \equiv y
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variables"} variables
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in A
                which satisfies reflexivity, transitivity, and symmetry has a quotient set
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ≡
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A/\equiv
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+schema"} axiom schema
                of quotient sets.
          %p
            In any case, the element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ≡
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S/{\equiv}
            that comes from the element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            may be denoted
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ≡
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [x]_{\equiv}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [x]
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≡
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\equiv}
            is understood, or simply
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            if there will be no confusion as to which set it is an element of. This
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [x]
            is called the
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+class"} equivalence class
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            with respect to
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≡
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \equiv
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:setdef"} (1)
            above, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [x]
            is literally the set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h4#as_initial_objects_in_a_category As initial objects in a category
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≡
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \equiv
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %em
              quotient set algebra of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≡
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \equiv
            to be a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            with a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ι
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota S \to A
            such that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in S
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ≡
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a \equiv b)
            implies
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\iota(a) = \iota(b))
          %p
            A
            %em
              quotient set algebra homomorphism of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≡
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \equiv
            is a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: A \to B
            between two quotient set algebras
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            such that for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in S
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\iota_A(a)) = \iota_B(a)
          %p
            The
            %em
              category of quotient set algebras of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≡
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \equiv
            is the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QSA
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ≡
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QSA(S, \equiv)
            whose objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi QSA
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ≡
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ob(QSA(S, \equiv))
            are quotient set algebras of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≡
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \equiv
            and whose morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(A, B)
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi QSA
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ≡
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Ob(QSA(S, \equiv))
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi QSA
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ≡
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \in Ob(QSA(S, \equiv))
            are quotient set algebra homomorphisms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≡
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \equiv
            %strong quotient set
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≡
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \equiv
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ≡
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S/\equiv
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≡
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \equiv
          %h3#in_dependent_type_theory In dependent type theory
          %p
            Similar to set theory, there are multiple ways of defining quotient sets in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent"} univalent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+all+propositions"} type of all propositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                  %mo ,
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathrm{Prop}, \mathrm{El})
            and thus
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+sets"} power sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒫
                  %mi T
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi T
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}T \coloneqq T \to \mathrm{Prop}
            of a type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            with an equivalence relation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≡
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ×
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)\equiv(-):\mathcal{P}(T \times T)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ≡
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T/\equiv
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subtype"} subtype
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicate"} predicate
            on the powerset
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}T
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒫
                  %mi T
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isEquivalenceClass
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi T
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo :
                        %mi T
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≡
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P:\mathcal{P}T \vdash \mathrm{isEquivalenceClass}(P) \coloneqq \left[\sum_{x:T} \prod_{y:T} P(x) =_\mathrm{Prop} (x \equiv y) \right]
          %p
            since by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} univalence
            there is an equivalence between the types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≡
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(x) =_\mathrm{Prop} (x \equiv y)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≡
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{El}(P(x)) \simeq \mathrm{El}(x \equiv y)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≡
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{El}(P(x)) \iff \mathrm{El}(x \equiv y)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ≡
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒫
                      %mi T
                  %mi isEquivalenceClass
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T/\equiv \coloneqq \sum_{P:\mathcal{P}T} isEquivalenceClass(P)
          %p
            Alternatively, if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            does not have a type of all propositions, then the quotient set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ≡
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T/\equiv
            can still nevertheless be constructed. The analogue of the axiom of quotient sets in dependent type theory is the rules for the quotient set
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+type"} higher inductive type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ≡
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T/\equiv
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+type"} higher inductive type
            inductively generated by the following:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ι
                      %mo :
                      %mi T
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ≡
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota: T \to T/\equiv
            %li
              %p a family of dependent terms
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi T
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi T
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi eq
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo ≡
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo →
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ι
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo ≡
                      %mi ι
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      a \colon T
                      ,\;
                      b \colon T
                      \\;\;\; \vdash \;\;\;
                      eq_{T/\equiv}(a, b)
                      \\,\colon\,
                      (a \equiv b)
                      \\;\to\;
                      (\iota(a) =_{T/\equiv} \iota(b))
            %li
              %p a family of dependent terms
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ≡
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ≡
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi τ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi isProp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo ≡
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:T/\equiv, b:T/\equiv \vdash \tau(a, b): isProp(a =_{T/\equiv} b)
          %p
            In general, if one doesn’t have impredicative quotient sets or quotient sets as a higher inductive type, than one could only construct quotient sets of equivalence relations with a choice of unique representatives, which for equivalence relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x, y)
            indexed by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y:A
            consists of a type family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(x)
            indexed by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %mo ∃
                  %mo !
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo .
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{x:A} \exists!y:A.C(x) \times R(x, y)
          %p
            Then the type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{x:A} C(x)
            is the quotient set of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            with respect to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            Equivalently, one could use functions instead of type families, and say that a choice of unique representatives is a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:C \to A
            and an element of type
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %mo ∃
                  %mo !
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo .
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi z
                        %mo :
                        %mi C
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %mi x
                    %mo )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{x:A} \exists!y:A.\left(\sum_{z:C} f(z) =_A x\right) \times R(x, y)
          %p Then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ≃
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \simeq \sum_{x:A} \sum_{z:C} f(z) =_A x
          %p
            is the quotient set of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            with respect to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %h2#generalisations Generalisations
          %p
            Quotient sets in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            generalise to
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+object"} quotient object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+category"} exact category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
            in which every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence"} congruence
            on every object has an effective quotient object.
          %h2#see_also See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/setoid"} setoid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+type"} quotient type
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+type"} higher inductive type
          %h2#rereferences Rereferences
          %p
            For quotient sets in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"}> Egbert Rijke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Homotopy+Type+Theory"} Introduction to Homotopy Type Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.11082"} arXiv:2212.11082
          %p
            See the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+type"} quotient type
          .property
            category:
            %a.category_link{:href => "/nlab/all_pages/foundational+axiom"} foundational axiom
